e"><addressbook><name>NEC CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MARUMOTO TSUNEHISA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MARUMOTO, TSUNEHISA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>There are provided drive means for displacing a contact (11) according to a control signal (12), a first control signal line for passing a control signal to the drive means (4), and first signal blocking means (3) connected with the first control signal line for blocking a high-frequency signal flowing through a high-frequency signal line (1a, 1b). As a result, the insertion loss due to a micromachine switch is reduced, and the high-frequency characteristics of a circuit including a micromachine switch are improved.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un organe d'entraînement conçu pour déplacer un contact (11) en fonction d'un signal de commande (12), un premier conducteur de signal de commande destiné faire passer un signal de commande à l'organe d'entraînement (4), et un premier organe de blocage de signal (3) relié au premier conducteur de signal de commande destiné à bloquer un signal hautes fréquences traversant le conducteur de signal hautes fréquences (1a, 1b). La perte d'insertion due à un commutateur de micromachine est ainsi réduite, et les caractéristiques hautes fréquences d'un circuit comprenant un commutateur de micromachine sont améliorées.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but